    <text xml:lang="oic">
        <body>
            <pb n="37r"/>
            <lb n="24"/>
            <div n="1">
                <p>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>&lsqb;d&slongdes;&rsqb;vmleiz&slongdes;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>brynielfr</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>Brynj&oacute;lfr</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <note>The "e" following "l" makes more sense to be an "o", however the shape on the page appears closer to the execution of "e" that this hand takes. In the cipher used on 33v, "e" represents "c" which would make no sense here. Because the word "&thorn;etta" appears later in this sentence with an unchanged "e", I elect to keep "e" here in the diplomatic edition..</note>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>r&gsmlowloop;clm&slongdes;&xldes;b&xldes;&slongdes; &rflour;om</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>steinradar son</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>Steinr&aacute;&eth;arson</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>&slongdes;l&gsmlowloop;&xldes;bc</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>ritade</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>rita&eth;i</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>&thorn;e&gsmlowloop;&lsqb;&gsmlowloop;&xldes;&rsqb;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>&thorn;et&lsqb;ta&rsqb;</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>&thorn;etta</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>&etslash;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl><ex>og</ex></me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>ok</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>c&slong;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>er</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>er</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <lb n="25"/>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>&lsqb;c&rsqb;m&trot;o</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>engo</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>engu</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>mv&gsmlowloop;&gsmlowloop;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>nytt</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>n&yacute;tt</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <lb n="26"/>
                    <seg type="nb"> <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>l</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>i</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>&iacute;</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>&xldes;&inodot;&gsmlowloop;&lsqb;xs&rsqb;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>alt&lsqb;ar&rsqb;</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>altar</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w> </seg>
                    <note>The encoded ending "xs" from Kålund's edition does not reflect what I observed on the leaf. To me, the shapes looked closer to "y&rrot;", but "altus" would make little sense in the diplomatic in comparison to "altar".</note>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>q&xldes;&iacute;&iacute;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>pall</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>P&aacute;ll</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <seg type="nb"> <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>&xldes;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>a</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>&aacute;</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>nl&trot;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>mig</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>mik</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w> </seg>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>yc&iacute;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>uel</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>vel</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>m&xldes;&gsmlowloop;&gsmlowloop;y</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>mattu</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>m&aacute;ttu</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <note>Although an "m" is written in the cipher text, nattu would make little sense in the diplomatic edition. Therefore it is easier to think that the scribe made a mistake and did not encode "m" correctly.</note>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>rl&xldes;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>sia</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>sj&aacute;</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                    <w>
                        <choice>
                            <me:facs>&lsqb;nl&rsqb;&trot;</me:facs>
                            <me:dipl>&lsqb;mi&rsqb;g</me:dipl>
                            <me:norm>mik</me:norm>
                        </choice>
                    </w>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
